    "result": "Perfect! I've successfully implemented the `--threshold` feature for `frai eval`. Here's a summary of what was added:\n\n## Implementation Summary\n\n### Core Changes\n\n**1. `frai-core/src/eval/index.js` \u2013 Threshold Logic**\n- `parseThresholds(strs)` \u2013 Parses threshold strings like `\"exact_match=0.9\"` with validation for format and range (0-1)\n- `validateThresholds(thresholds, availableMetricIds)` \u2013 Ensures all threshold metrics exist\n- `evaluateThresholds(evaluations, thresholds)` \u2013 Evaluates metrics against thresholds, returns `{ passed, thresholds }`\n- Modified `generateReport()` \u2013 Accepts optional `thresholds` parameter and adds `passed` and `thresholds` fields to output\n\n**2. `frai-core/src/eval/reporters.js` \u2013 Report Output**\n- JSON: Adds top-level `passed` field and `thresholds` array to reports\n- Markdown: Adds \"## Thresholds\" section showing `PASS`/`FAIL` status with min/score for each\n\n**3. `frai-cli/src/index.ts` \u2013 CLI Integration**\n- Added `--threshold <metric>=<min>` option to `frai eval` (repeatable)\n- Parses, validates, and passes thresholds to `generateReport()`\n- Exit codes:\n  - `0` if all thresholds pass (or no thresholds specified)\n  - `1` if any threshold fails\n  - `2` if threshold format/metric is invalid\n\n**4. Tests** (`frai-core/src/eval/index.test.js`)\n- Comprehensive test coverage for parsing, validation, evaluation, and edge cases\n- Tests null scores and missing metrics (both fail thresholds as required)\n\n**5. Documentation**\n- Updated both `packages/frai-cli/README.md` and `packages/frai-core/README.md`\n- Added SDK example showing programmatic threshold usage\n\n## Behavior\n\n- A metric with no score (null) **fails** the threshold instead of crashing or passing\n- Reports are always written, with threshold results included\n- Works with custom metrics passed to `runEvaluations`\n- Without `--threshold`, reports and exit codes behave exactly as they do today\n\nThe feature is ready for testing. You can use it like:\n```bash\nfrai eval --outputs results.json --references refs.json --threshold exact_match=0.9 --threshold toxicity=1.0\n```",
